From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:20:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: hand the guest a new texture zeroed

A guest allocates the pages behind a new texture zeroed, and expects to
read zeros from the texture until it writes it. The texture's own
storage is memory the host driver hands out again once another resource
has released it, with that resource's pixels still in it. A texture the
renderer leaves as it finds it therefore shows what an earlier one held,
which may have belonged to another guest process, and a pair of fresh
buffers differ although neither was written. Android's
BitmapTest#testSameAs_wrappedHardwareBuffer compares such a pair.

Clear every level of a texture the renderer creates with glClearTexImage
and no data, when the driver offers it. A texture imported from an image
keeps the content it was imported with.

A compressed format cannot be cleared that way, and writing zero blocks
over the whole texture makes the driver stage them in buffers as large
as the texture, held until the context reuses that batch state and
refused when the device memory budget is full. The zero blocks are
written once instead, into a tile: a texture of the same format as large
as the first level up to 128 x 128 blocks (256 KiB for 16-byte blocks),
uploaded in calls of at most 16 KiB. Every level and layer then receives
its whole blocks by glCopyImageSubData from the tile, a copy between
textures of one format that Metal does without a staging buffer. Only
the part block at the right and bottom edge of a level whose size is not
a whole number of blocks, and a level smaller than one block, are
uploaded, at most 16 KiB a call, for every layer. The tile is deleted
before the texture is returned. The texture then holds zero blocks,
which the format decodes as it defines, not always to a zero texel: sRGB
ASTC samples as its error colour.

A step the driver refuses room for raises GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY: the tile, an
upload, a copy. It fails the creation with ENOMEM, as a refused storage
does, so the request meets the reclaim and retry, and a texture the
fill left partly written is released and never reaches the guest. A
host without glCopyImageSubData leaves a compressed texture as the
driver finds it.

Cost on an M1 Ultra under load, creating thread, main against this:
0.01 -> 0.2 ms for a 256x256 ETC2 texture with its levels and for ASTC
4x4 at 1024x1024, 0.01 -> 0.9 ms for a cube, 0.01 -> 15 to 20 ms for
a 256-layer array and 0.01 -> 40 to 60 ms for a 4096-high array one
to five texels wide, with 512 layers. The cost is a copy for each layer
and level. Copying the layers from the first, or by doubling, was
measured as well, on Zink over KosmicKrisp, which does a Metal copy per
layer. The per-layer loop is kept because it is best or tied on the
costly shapes, the 256-layer ETC2 array and the narrow arrays; the
others win only on cubes, which take under a millisecond. The Mesa
fallback path of the others was not run. The GPU needs 0.4 to 0.7 ms
more for a 2D texture before it is finished. Nothing is paid once the
texture exists.

The driver holds the tile (256 KiB at most) and the staging of its
upload, as much again, and the staging of the part block uploads, which
grow with the layers: the Metal allocation of a 1 x 4096 x 512 ASTC 4x4
array is 4 MiB above its 8 MiB, and that of a 1022 x 1022 x 64 array
with levels 8 MiB above its 86 MiB. A released compressed texture is
freed when its context next reuses the batch state of its zeroing, is
trimmed as idle, or a refused creation reclaims, not at once. The
command storage of the copies is counted by the memory pool but cannot
be refused: it measured 22 to 26 MiB straight after the creation of a
1022 x 1022 x 64 ASTC 4x4 array with levels and of a 256 x 256 x 256
one. A large layered compressed texture therefore needs about that much
room beyond its size, or its creation is refused with ENOMEM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 205 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 205 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index daef37018d3e4092a8ce14698c43150acd391d37..4362b457638ec5b7d8744a65e69828fe7d89a4bf 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -9470,6 +9470,202 @@ vrend_resource_create(const struct vrend_renderer_resource_create_args *args)
    return gr;
 }
 
+static uint32_t vrend_get_texture_depth(struct vrend_resource *res, uint32_t level);
+
+/* Zero blocks for the parts of a new compressed texture that are written by
+ * an upload: the tile the rest is copied from, and the part block at the edge
+ * of a level. One call writes at most this much, so the driver stages at
+ * most this much for it. */
+static const uint8_t vrend_zero_blocks[16 * 1024];
+
+/* The most blocks along one side of the tile a compressed texture is zeroed
+ * from: 128 x 128 blocks of 16 bytes is 256 KiB. */
+#define VREND_ZERO_TILE_BLOCKS 128
+
+/* Upload zero blocks over a part of one layer of a level: a face of a cube,
+ * a slice of an array or a volume. */
+static void vrend_zero_compressed_part(struct vrend_resource *gr,
+                                       GLenum internalformat, uint32_t level,
+                                       uint32_t layer, uint32_t x, uint32_t y,
+                                       uint32_t width, uint32_t height,
+                                       uint32_t blocks)
+{
+   const GLsizei size = blocks * util_format_get_blocksize(gr->base.format);
+
+   if (gr->target == GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP)
+      glCompressedTexSubImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP_POSITIVE_X + layer, level,
+                                x, y, width, height, internalformat, size,
+                                vrend_zero_blocks);
+   else if (gr->target == GL_TEXTURE_2D)
+      glCompressedTexSubImage2D(gr->target, level, x, y, width, height,
+                                internalformat, size, vrend_zero_blocks);
+   else
+      glCompressedTexSubImage3D(gr->target, level, x, y, layer, width, height,
+                                1, internalformat, size, vrend_zero_blocks);
+}
+
+/* Write zero blocks over every level and layer of a new compressed texture,
+ * as vrend_resource_zero_texture clears the others. A compressed format
+ * cannot be cleared, and uploading zero blocks over the whole texture makes
+ * the driver stage them in buffers as large as the texture, which it holds
+ * until its context reuses that batch state and a full device memory budget
+ * refuses. So the zero blocks are written once, into a tile: a texture of the
+ * same format as large as the first level up to 128 x 128 blocks (256 KiB
+ * for 16-byte blocks), uploaded in calls of at most 16 KiB. The whole blocks
+ * of every level and layer are then copied from the tile on the GPU, a copy
+ * between textures of one format that needs no staging. Only the part block
+ * at the right and bottom edge of a level whose size is not a whole number of
+ * blocks, and a level smaller than one block in either direction, are
+ * uploaded, at most 16 KiB a call, once for every layer.
+ *
+ * What the driver holds for this beyond the texture is the tile (256 KiB at
+ * most) and the staging of its upload (as much again), and the staging of
+ * every part block upload, until the context reuses that batch state or is
+ * trimmed. The part blocks of one layer take 256 KiB at most, but a texture
+ * with many layers stages them all: a level narrower than one block stages
+ * its whole image once for every layer, which is 8 MiB for an ASTC 4x4 array
+ * 1 texel wide, 4096 high and 512 deep. Copying the layers from the first
+ * instead stages one layer's part blocks, and costs more creation time.
+ *
+ * Returns false when the driver refused one of the steps, which leaves the
+ * texture partly written: the caller releases it and reports ENOMEM, so that
+ * the guest's request meets the reclaim and retry a refused storage does. An
+ * upload the driver refuses raises GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY (it fails to map the
+ * texture), and a copy allocates nothing on the product hosts. A host that
+ * cannot copy images leaves the texture as the driver gave it, and returns
+ * true.
+ */
+static bool vrend_resource_zero_compressed(struct vrend_resource *gr)
+{
+   const enum virgl_formats fmt = gr->base.format;
+   const GLenum internalformat = tex_conv_table[fmt].internalformat;
+   const uint32_t blocksize = util_format_get_blocksize(fmt);
+   const uint32_t block_width = util_format_get_blockwidth(fmt);
+   const uint32_t block_height = util_format_get_blockheight(fmt);
+   const uint32_t max_blocks = sizeof(vrend_zero_blocks) / blocksize;
+   const bool cube = gr->target == GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP;
+   const bool layered = gr->target == GL_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY ||
+                        gr->target == GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP_ARRAY ||
+                        gr->target == GL_TEXTURE_3D;
+
+   if (!has_feature(feat_copy_image) || !internalformat ||
+       blocksize > sizeof(vrend_zero_blocks) ||
+       (gr->target != GL_TEXTURE_2D && !cube && !layered))
+      return true;
+
+   const uint32_t tile_w = MIN2(gr->base.width0 / block_width,
+                                VREND_ZERO_TILE_BLOCKS);
+   const uint32_t tile_h = MIN2(gr->base.height0 / block_height,
+                                VREND_ZERO_TILE_BLOCKS);
+   GLuint tile = 0;
+
+   vrend_drain_gl_errors();
+   if (tile_w && tile_h) {
+      glGenTextures(1, &tile);
+      glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, tile);
+      glTexStorage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 1, internalformat, tile_w * block_width,
+                     tile_h * block_height);
+      const uint32_t rows_per_call = max_blocks / tile_w;
+      for (uint32_t row = 0; row < tile_h; row += rows_per_call) {
+         const uint32_t rows = MIN2(rows_per_call, tile_h - row);
+         glCompressedTexSubImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, 0, row * block_height,
+                                   tile_w * block_width,
+                                   rows * block_height, internalformat,
+                                   rows * tile_w * blocksize,
+                                   vrend_zero_blocks);
+      }
+      glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0);
+      if (vrend_storage_refused("a compressed texture's zero tile")) {
+         glDeleteTextures(1, &tile);
+         return false;
+      }
+   }
+
+   glBindTexture(gr->target, gr->gl_id);
+   for (uint32_t level = 0; level <= gr->base.last_level; level++) {
+      const uint32_t width = u_minify(gr->base.width0, level);
+      const uint32_t height = u_minify(gr->base.height0, level);
+      const uint32_t whole_x = width / block_width;
+      const uint32_t whole_y = height / block_height;
+      const uint32_t blocks_y = util_format_get_nblocksy(fmt, height);
+      const uint32_t depth = vrend_get_texture_depth(gr, level);
+
+      for (uint32_t layer = 0; layer < depth; layer++) {
+         for (uint32_t by = 0; tile && by < whole_y; by += tile_h) {
+            for (uint32_t bx = 0; bx < whole_x; bx += tile_w)
+               glCopyImageSubData(tile, GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, 0, 0, 0,
+                                  gr->gl_id, gr->target, level,
+                                  bx * block_width, by * block_height, layer,
+                                  MIN2(tile_w, whole_x - bx) * block_width,
+                                  MIN2(tile_h, whole_y - by) * block_height,
+                                  1);
+         }
+
+         /* The column of part blocks at the right edge, down to the corner. */
+         if (width % block_width) {
+            const uint32_t x = whole_x * block_width;
+            for (uint32_t by = 0; by < blocks_y; by += max_blocks) {
+               const uint32_t n = MIN2(max_blocks, blocks_y - by);
+               const uint32_t y = by * block_height;
+               vrend_zero_compressed_part(gr, internalformat, level, layer, x,
+                                          y, width - x,
+                                          MIN2(n * block_height, height - y),
+                                          n);
+            }
+         }
+
+         /* The row of part blocks at the bottom edge, left of the corner. */
+         if (height % block_height) {
+            const uint32_t y = whole_y * block_height;
+            for (uint32_t bx = 0; bx < whole_x; bx += max_blocks) {
+               const uint32_t n = MIN2(max_blocks, whole_x - bx);
+               vrend_zero_compressed_part(gr, internalformat, level, layer,
+                                          bx * block_width, y,
+                                          n * block_width, height - y, n);
+            }
+         }
+      }
+   }
+   glBindTexture(gr->target, 0);
+   if (tile)
+      glDeleteTextures(1, &tile);
+   return !vrend_storage_refused("a compressed texture's zero blocks");
+}
+
+/* The storage of a new texture is memory the host driver hands out again once
+ * another resource - possibly another guest process's - has released it, and
+ * the guest allocated zeroed pages for the same resource. Fill a texture the
+ * renderer created with zeros before the guest can read it, so the guest sees
+ * what it allocated and never another resource's pixels. An imported image
+ * keeps the content it was imported with. A compressed texture is filled with
+ * zero blocks, which the format decodes as it defines. Returns false when the
+ * driver refused room for the fill of a compressed texture.
+ */
+static bool vrend_resource_zero_texture(struct vrend_resource *gr)
+{
+   const enum virgl_formats fmt = gr->base.format;
+   const GLenum format = tex_conv_table[fmt].glformat;
+   const GLenum type = tex_conv_table[fmt].gltype;
+
+   if (!has_bit(gr->storage_bits, VREND_STORAGE_GL_TEXTURE) ||
+       has_bit(gr->storage_bits, VREND_STORAGE_EGL_IMAGE))
+      return true;
+
+   if (util_format_is_compressed(fmt))
+      return vrend_resource_zero_compressed(gr);
+
+   if (!has_feature(feat_clear_texture) || !format || !type)
+      return true;
+
+   for (uint32_t level = 0; level <= gr->base.last_level; level++) {
+      if (vrend_state.use_gles)
+         glClearTexImageEXT(gr->gl_id, level, format, type, NULL);
+      else
+         glClearTexImage(gr->gl_id, level, format, type, NULL);
+   }
+   return true;
+}
+
 struct pipe_resource *
 vrend_renderer_resource_create(const struct vrend_renderer_resource_create_args *args,
                                void *image_oes)
@@ -9486,6 +9682,15 @@ vrend_renderer_resource_create(const struct vrend_renderer_resource_create_args
    } else {
       const enum virgl_formats format = gr->base.format;
       ret = vrend_resource_alloc_texture(gr, format, image_oes);
+      if (!ret && !image_oes && !vrend_resource_zero_texture(gr)) {
+         /* A texture the fill left partly written is released, as one whose
+          * storage was refused is, and the request is refused for room. */
+         glDeleteTextures(1, &gr->gl_id);
+         gr->gl_id = 0;
+         gr->storage_bits &= ~(VREND_STORAGE_GL_TEXTURE |
+                               VREND_STORAGE_GL_IMMUTABLE);
+         ret = ENOMEM;
+      }
    }
 
    if (ret) {
